  43: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  44:     """
  45:     Reverse the sequence of colors along the single 4-connected foreground path while keeping the path shape fixed.
  46: 
  47:     Input structure:
  48:     - The background is the dominant color.
  49:     - All non-background pixels form one multicolor 4-connected one-pixel-wide path.
  50:     - The path has exactly two endpoints and no branches.
  51: 
  52:     Rule:
  53:     - Walk the path from one endpoint to the other.
  54:     - Replace the colors on those same path cells by the original path colors in reverse order.
  55:     - Leave every background pixel unchanged.
  56: 
  57:     Key insight:
  58:     - Nothing moves geometrically; only the color string written on the path is reversed between the endpoints.
